Unknown command: --version
Tina4 Ruby CLI

Usage: tina4ruby COMMAND [options]

Commands:
  init [NAME]                                     Initialize a new Tina4 project
  start [options]                                 Start the Tina4 web server
  serve                                           Alias for start
  migrate [--create NAME] [--rollback N]          Run database migrations
  migrate:create <desc>                           Create a new migration file
  migrate:status                                  Show migration status (completed and pending)
  migrate:rollback [-n N]                         Rollback the last batch of migrations
  seed [--clear]                                  Run all seed files in seeds/
  seed:create NAME                                Create a new seed file
  test                                            Run inline tests
  queue <work|stats|retry|clear> [topic]          Run queue workers and manage jobs
  build [--tag NAME] [--file PATH]                Build the deployable Docker image
  lint [--fix] [--no-install]                     Lint src/ + app.rb (rubocop, installed dev-only on demand, else ruby -c)
  version                                         Show Tina4 version
  routes                                          List all registered routes
  console                                         Start an interactive console
  generate <what> <name> [options]                Generate scaffolding (see Generators below)
  ai [--all]                                      Detect AI tools and install context files
  commands [--json]                               List available commands (add --json for machine form)
  help                                            Show this help message

Delegated to the tina4 client (same behaviour in every framework):
  doctor                                          Check installed languages and tools
  setup                                           Guided, menu-driven setup: install everything + scaffold a ready-to-run project
  deploy <docker|systemd|nginx|cpanel> [--force]  Generate deployment scaffolding (Dockerfile, systemd unit, nginx block, cPanel)
  (these run the tina4 client — install: curl -fsSL https://tina4.com/install.sh | sh)

Generators:
  generate model <Name> [--fields "name:string,price:float"] [--table-name <name>]  ORM model + matching migration
  generate route <name> [--model Name] [--public]  CRUD route file, secure by default (--public opens writes)
  generate crud <Name> [--fields "..."] [--public]  Model + migration + routes + form + view + test
  generate migration <description>                Timestamped migration file (UP/DOWN)
  generate middleware <Name>                      Middleware with before/after hooks
  generate test <name> [--model Name]             RSpec test file
  generate form <Name> [--fields "..."]           Form template with inputs matching model fields
  generate view <Name> [--fields "..."]           List + detail view templates
  generate auth                                   Login/register routes + User model + templates
  generate service <Name> [--every 5m | --cron "..."]  Scheduled ServiceRunner task (src/services/)
  generate queue <topic>                          Producer + consumer worker (src/services/)
  generate validator <Name>                       Request-body Validator (src/validators/)
  generate seeder <Model>                         FakeData + seed_orm seeder (seeds/)
  generate websocket <path>                       Tina4.websocket handler (src/routes/)
  generate listener <event>                       Tina4::Events.on listener (src/listeners/)

Scaffolding-first: logic-shaped generators (route without --model, service,
queue, validator, seeder, websocket, listener) emit wiring + an AI-FILL
placeholder (raise NotImplementedError) where the custom logic goes; CRUD-
shaped ones emit working code. Writes are secure by default; use --public
to open them.

Field types: string, int, float, bool, text, datetime, blob
Table names: singular by default (Product -> product)

https://tina4.com

Run 'tina4ruby COMMAND --help' for more information on a command.
